#: landing/templates/faq.html:23
msgid ""
"\n"
"        <p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: var(--mq-txt-"
"color, #BB285C);\" id=\"about-lut-kyyti\">About LUT Kyyti</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Who "
"can use LUT Kyyti?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">LUT Kyyti is intended for LUT and LAB employees. Access is limited to "
"users with a verified LUT or LAB email address.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">During the pilot phase, the "
"service is not available to the general public.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">How "
"does LUT Kyyti work?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">Drivers post rides they are already planning to make. Passengers can "
"search for suitable rides and request to join them.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Passengers can also post ride "
"requests when they are looking for a ride. The driver and passenger then "
"agree on practical details such as the exact pickup point and timing.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"bold;\">Is LUT Kyyti a taxi or transport service?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No. LUT Kyyti is not a taxi, "
"bus, or transport provider.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">It is a platform that helps members of the LUT and LAB "
"community find other people travelling in the same direction. LUT Kyyti does "
"not operate vehicles or employ drivers.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Does LUT Kyyti plan routes "
"for me?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No. LUT "
"Kyyti does not provide route planning.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drivers and passengers enter their own trip "
"details, including the departure area, destination, date, and time.</span></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Can students use LUT Kyyti?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">During the pilot phase, LUT Kyyti is available only to LUT "
"and LAB employees.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">The service may later be opened to LUT and LAB students after the "
"pilot has been successfully completed and evaluated.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Can "
"I use LUT Kyyti for trips other than commuting?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The main purpose of LUT Kyyti "
"is to support commuting to and from LUT and LAB campuses and workplaces.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Other suitable "
"trips may also be allowed, depending on the service rules during the pilot.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"bold;\">Why should I use LUT Kyyti?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">LUT Kyyti can help reduce commuting costs, make "
"everyday travel more social, and lower transport-related emissions by "
"filling empty seats in vehicles already making the journey.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can learn more on the </"
"span>\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/faq.html:26
msgid "Impact page"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/faq.html:27
msgid ""
"\n"
"        <p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: var(--mq-txt-"
"color, #B70F0A);\" id=\"accounts-and-privacy\">Accounts and privacy</span></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Is my LUT/LAB account connected to my LUT Kyyti account?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No. Your LUT Kyyti account is "
"separate from your LUT or LAB user account.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You register using your LUT or LAB email address "
"and create a separate password for LUT Kyyti.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Can "
"I use my LUT/LAB account password for LUT Kyyti?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You should not reuse your LUT "
"or LAB account password.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">Create a separate and unique password for LUT Kyyti. LUT "
"Kyyti will never ask for your LUT or LAB account password.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">How "
"is my LUT/LAB email address verified?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When registering, you will be asked to verify "
"your LUT or LAB email address.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">Verification confirms that you are eligible to use the "
"service. Follow the instructions sent to your email address to complete the "
"registration process.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">What should I do if I forget "
"my password?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Use "
"the password reset option on the login page.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A password reset message will be sent to the "
"email address connected to your LUT Kyyti account.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Do I "
"need to provide my home address?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No. LUT Kyyti does not ask you to provide your "
"home address.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">When posting a trip, you can enter a city, town, neighbourhood, "
"campus, or another suitable meeting area as the departure point. You and the "
"other rider can agree on the exact pickup location separately.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">What "
"information can other users see about me?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Other users may see limited information needed "
"to arrange a trip, such as your first name and relevant trip details.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your contact "
"information is shared according to the contact preferences you select and "
"the way the service is configured. Exact visibility rules should be "
"explained in the Privacy Policy.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">How can I communicate with "
"another rider?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">When creating your account, you may be asked to provide contact "
"information such as your email address and phone number.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can choose which "
"available contact methods other riders may use. Drivers and passengers are "
"responsible for agreeing on practical details directly with each other.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"bold;\">Can I delete my LUT Kyyti account?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. You can request the deletion of your LUT "
"Kyyti account and associated personal information.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Some information may need to "
"be retained for a limited period where required by law or for legitimate "
"administrative, security, or dispute-resolution purposes. Further "
"information is available in the Privacy Policy.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">What "
"happens to my account if I leave LUT or LAB?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">LUT Kyyti is intended for current LUT and LAB "
"community members.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">If you no longer have an eligible LUT or LAB email address or "
"employment relationship, your access may be restricted or your account may "
"be closed in accordance with the Terms of Service.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p>\n"
"        <p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: var(--mq-txt-"
"color, rgb(187, 40, 92));\" id=\"posting-and-joining-trips\">Posting and "
"joining trips</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Can I offer a recurring ride?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. If you regularly commute "
"on the same route, you can post a recurring ride so others can join when "
"suitable.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Make "
"sure the days, times, and recurrence details are accurate and update the "
"ride if your schedule changes.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Can I join a ride as a "
"passenger?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. "
"You can browse available rides and request to join a ride that matches your "
"travel needs.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A "
"ride is not necessarily confirmed until the driver accepts your request.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"bold;\">Can I post a ride request?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. If you cannot find a suitable posted ride, "
"you can create a ride request describing where and when you would like to "
"travel.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Other "
"users can then respond if they are able to offer a suitable ride.</span></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Can I look for travel companions for train, bus, or taxi trips?</span></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. You can also post a "
"trip if you are looking for other people to share public transport or taxi "
"travel.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The "
"users are responsible for making the booking and agreeing on any costs "
"directly with each other.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Does a driver have to accept "
"every passenger request?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">No. Drivers can decide whether to accept or decline a "
"passenger request.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">They may consider factors such as available seats, pickup "
"arrangements, timing, and whether the requested trip fits their planned "
"route.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: bold;\">How many passengers can join a ride?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The driver decides how many "
"seats are available and enters this information when posting the ride.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The number of "
"accepted passengers should not exceed the available seating capacity of the "
"vehicle.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: bold;\">What happens after I request to join a ride?</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The driver "
"reviews the request and can accept or decline it.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once the request is accepted, "
"the driver and passenger can agree on the exact pickup point, timing, and "
"any other practical arrangements.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">How will I know if someone "
"requests to join my ride?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">LUT Kyyti will notify you through the notification methods "
"available in the service.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">You should also check your account regularly for new requests "
"and changes to existing trips.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Who decides the pickup and "
"drop-off points?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">The driver sets the main trip details when posting the ride.</span></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The driver and passenger "
"can then agree on suitable pickup and drop-off arrangements. Neither person "
"is required to share their home address.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Can I edit or delete a "
"trip after posting it?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">Yes. You can update or remove a trip if your plans change.</span></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If another user has "
"already requested or agreed to join the trip, inform them as early as "
"possible about any changes or cancellation.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Can I cancel a ride or "
"passenger request?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">Yes. Plans can change, and both drivers and passengers may cancel.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cancel as early "
"as possible and inform the other person so they have time to make "
"alternative arrangements.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">What if the driver or "
"passenger is late?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">Drivers and passengers are responsible for communicating with each "
"other.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Agree on "
"the timing clearly in advance and contact the other person as soon as "
"possible if you expect to be late.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p>\n"
"        <p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: var(--mq-txt-"
"color, rgb(187, 40, 92));\" id=\"costs-and-payments\">Costs and payments</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"bold;\">Is using LUT Kyyti free?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. Using the LUT Kyyti platform is free.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Any cost sharing "
"between the driver and passenger, such as a contribution towards fuel costs, "
"is agreed directly between the users.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Does LUT Kyyti handle "
"payments?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No. "
"LUT Kyyti does not process or collect payments.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drivers and passengers are "
"responsible for agreeing on any possible cost sharing and arranging payment "
"directly with each other.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">How should ride costs be "
"shared?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Any "
"contribution should be agreed before the trip.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The purpose of LUT Kyyti is "
"to support shared travel, not commercial passenger transport. Drivers are "
"responsible for ensuring that any cost-sharing arrangement complies with "
"applicable laws, insurance terms, and tax rules.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p>\n"
"        <p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: var(--mq-txt-"
"color, rgb(187, 40, 92));\" id=\"safety-and-responsibilities\">Safety and "
"responsibilities</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Is LUT Kyyti safe to use?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">LUT Kyyti is intended for "
"verified LUT and LAB community members, which makes it different from an "
"open public marketplace.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">However, verification does not guarantee another user’s "
"behaviour, driving ability, identity beyond the information verified by the "
"service, or the safety of a particular trip. Users should use normal care "
"when arranging and sharing rides.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Who is responsible for the "
"vehicle and the journey?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">The driver is responsible for the vehicle, driving licence, "
"insurance, roadworthiness, legal compliance, and safe operation of the "
"vehicle.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">Passengers are responsible for behaving appropriately and following "
"reasonable safety instructions. LUT Kyyti only helps users find and contact "
"each other.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Does LUT Kyyti provide insurance?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No additional vehicle, "
"passenger, accident, or travel insurance is provided by LUT Kyyti unless "
"explicitly stated otherwise.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-"
"weight: 400;\">Drivers should ensure that their vehicle insurance covers the "
"planned journey and any permitted cost-sharing arrangement.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">What "
"should I do if I feel uncomfortable about a ride?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Do not join or continue with "
"a ride if you feel uncomfortable or believe the situation may be unsafe.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You may cancel "
"the arrangement, leave the ride when it is safe to do so, and contact the "
"LUT Kyyti team to report your concern.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In an emergency, contact the appropriate "
"emergency services.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: bold;\">What should I do if another user does not "
"arrive?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try to "
"contact the person using the agreed contact method.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If they do not respond, make "
"alternative travel arrangements where possible. Repeated no-shows or misuse "
"of the service can be reported to the LUT Kyyti team.</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Can "
"I report inappropriate behaviour or misuse?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. You should report harassment, threatening "
"behaviour, unsafe driving, misleading trip information, repeated no-shows, "
"misuse of personal information, or other violations of the service rules.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Reports can be "
"submitted through the contact or reporting method provided by LUT Kyyti.</"
"span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"bold;\">Can LUT Kyyti suspend or remove a user account?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. Access may be "
"restricted, suspended, or removed if a user violates the Terms of Service, "
"misuses the platform, provides misleading information, or creates safety or "
"security concerns.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: "
"400;\">Any action will be handled in accordance with the Terms of Service "
"and applicable university procedures.</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p>\n"
"        <p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: var(--mq-txt-"
"color, rgb(187, 40, 92));\" id=\"help-and-support\">Help and support</span></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Where can I find instructions for using LUT Kyyti?</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Detailed instructions for "
"using account features, posting trips, joining rides, managing requests, and "
"changing settings are available on the Help page after you log in.</span></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Who can I contact for help or feedback?</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can contact the LUT Kyyti team through the </"
"span>\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

