#: landing/templates/impact.html:6 landing/templates/index.html:36
#: landing/templates/landing.html:43 landing/templates/landing.html:81
msgid "Impact"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/impact.html:9
msgid "Why LUT Kyyti?"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/impact.html:12
msgid ""
"LUT University aims to reach net zero by 2050 and is working systematically "
"to reduce the climate impact of its operations. One important part of this "
"work is everyday mobility: how staff and students travel to and from campus."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/impact.html:16
msgid ""
"Staff and student commuting is one of the largest sources of LUT "
"University’s carbon footprint, accounting for around a third of total "
"emissions. LUT’s Climate Action Plan 2025–2030 recognises commuting as a key "
"area for action and includes measures to support more sustainable travel "
"choices, such as cooperation with campus cities and transport providers, "
"incentives for sustainable commuting, parking management, cycling support, "
"and awareness-raising."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/impact.html:20
msgid ""
"LUT Kyyti is one practical step in this direction. The service helps LUT and "
"LAB community members find others travelling in the same direction, so that "
"existing car journeys can be shared instead of made alone. While the long-"
"term electrification of private commuting will reduce emissions, sharing "
"rides can already help make current commuting more efficient by filling "
"empty seats in cars that are already making the trip."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/impact.html:24
msgid ""
"The impact of LUT Kyyti is not only environmental. Sharing commutes can also "
"help colleagues from different departments, campuses, and functions get to "
"know each other. In this way, LUT Kyyti can support a stronger sense of "
"community while contributing to LUT’s climate goals."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/impact.html:28
msgid ""
"Every shared ride is a small step, but together these choices can make a "
"meaningful difference. By offering a seat, joining a colleague’s ride, or "
"simply checking whether someone is travelling the same way, LUT and LAB "
"community members can help reduce commuting emissions and make everyday "
"travel more connected."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/index.html:11
msgid "Share your commute with LUT Kyyti"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/index.html:12
msgid ""
