#: landing/templates/safety.html:9
msgid "Safety and Ride Etiquette"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/safety.html:11
msgid ""
"\n"
"        <p dir=\"auto\">LUT Kyyti helps members of the LUT and LAB community "
"find others travelling in the same direction. To keep the service useful, "
"respectful, and safe for everyone, users are expected to communicate "
"clearly, behave responsibly, and use normal care when arranging shared rides."
"</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">LUT Kyyti is not a taxi, bus, or "
"transport service. It is a platform for connecting verified users. Drivers "
"and passengers are responsible for agreeing on the practical details of each "
"ride between themselves.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Before sharing a ride</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">Before joining or offering a ride, make "
"sure the key details are clear. These may include:</p><ul "
"dir=\"auto\"><li>departure point and destination</li><li>pickup and drop-off "
"location</li><li>date and time</li><li>whether the time is flexible</"
"li><li>return-trip details, if relevant</li><li>possible cost sharing</"
"li><li>luggage or special arrangements</li><li>how to contact each other if "
"plans change</li></ul><p dir=\"auto\">Do not assume that all details are "
"understood automatically. A short confirmation message before the ride can "
"help avoid confusion.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Communication</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\">Be polite, clear, and timely when communicating with other "
"users.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">If you are offering a "
"ride, describe the trip accurately. If you are requesting a ride, explain "
"what you need clearly. If plans change, inform the other person as early as "
"possible.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">Users should not "
"pressure others to accept a ride, change their route, share personal "
"information, or continue with an arrangement they are not comfortable with.</"
"p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Cost sharing</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">LUT Kyyti "
"does not handle payments. Any possible cost sharing is agreed directly "
"between the driver and passenger.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\">If cost sharing is expected, agree on it before the ride. The "
"amount should be reasonable and related to sharing travel costs, such as "
"fuel or parking. LUT Kyyti should not be used as a commercial taxi or "
"transport service.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span "
"style=\"font-weight: bold;\">During the ride</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></"
"p><p dir=\"auto\">Drivers and passengers should behave respectfully during "
"the trip.</p><p dir=\"auto\">Please be on time, keep the vehicle clean, and "
"respect the other person’s preferences. For example, agree before the ride "
"if there are questions about music, food, pets, smoking, luggage, or other "
"arrangements.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">Drivers are "
"responsible for driving safely and following traffic laws. Passengers should "
"not distract the driver or ask the driver to take unsafe actions.</p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">If "
"you are late or need to cancel</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\">Plans can change. If you are late or need to cancel, tell the "
"other person as soon as possible.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\">Repeated late cancellations, no-shows, or unclear communication "
"make the service less reliable for everyone. Please respect the other "
"person’s time and travel needs.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Personal safety</span></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">LUT Kyyti is intended for verified LUT/"
"LAB users, which makes it different from an open public marketplace. Users "
"should still use normal care when arranging shared rides.</p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">If something feels wrong, you are not "
"required to join or continue with a ride. You can decline a ride, change "
"your plans, or leave the situation if you feel uncomfortable.</p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">When meeting another user for the first "
"time, you may choose a clear and familiar pickup location, such as a campus "
"area, public transport station, or other public place.</p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Privacy and personal information</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\">Only share personal information that is necessary for arranging "
"the ride. Do not share another user’s contact details, travel plans, or "
"personal information with others without permission.</p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">Use the contact information available "
"through LUT Kyyti only for arranging rides or related communication.</p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Reporting concerns</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">If "
"you experience inappropriate behaviour, repeated no-shows, misuse of the "
"service, or anything that makes you feel unsafe, please contact the LUT "
"Kyyti team.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\">In urgent situations "
"or emergencies, contact the appropriate emergency services directly.</p><p "
"dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;"
"\">Shared responsibility</span></p><p dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p "
"dir=\"auto\">LUT Kyyti works best when users treat each other with respect "
"and communicate clearly. By using the service, you help create a more "
"practical, social, and climate-friendly commuting culture within the LUT and "
"LAB community.</p>\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

